f 17592186045417] [17592186265996 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265996 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "837dfba2-f78f-5c76-b27f-bb2d2c133624" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265996 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265997 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186265519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265997 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130862" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265997 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265997 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265997 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a5d6a7d0-f153-5a48-8ab8-2274611f50fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186265997 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the three given elementary row operations. \n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to apply the third elementary row operation to ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{3}$ on the left and get ${E}_{3}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326961 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{1}:=-4{R}_{1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326961 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326961 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "026c7004-8494-5ac7-b146-bd83da70b93c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327064 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327064 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327064 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0ef54140-2672-5265-b691-9d3fb2cd1f4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327342 #edb/ref 1080 "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327342 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327342 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2dc553fa-6372-54a1-80cf-6f418a317470" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327347 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327347 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327347 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2e06b7d4-773b-593e-9815-139447a16f89" #edb/re